<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
  <head>
    <meta http-equiv="content-type" content="text/html; charset=UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Baliadanga Girls' High School</title>
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin="">
    <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Poppins:wght@400;600;700&amp;display=swap"

      rel="stylesheet">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="style.css">
  </head>
  <body>
    <header>
      <h1>✨ Computer Resources ✨</h1>
      <p>Developing Computer Literacy </p>
    </header>
    <p>We have total of 5 laptops in our setup<br>
      *2 are HP laptops.<br>
      *3 are Dell laptops.<br>
      Computers/brand<br>
      *HP Laptops 2 Units:Modern HP laptops Model:HP 15-fd0xxx.<br>
      *Dell Laptops 3 Units: Older model Dell laptops.<br>
      Computer hardware specifications:<br>
      *HP Laptops Modern Setup:<br>
      *Processor type and speed:Intel Core i3 13 th Generation<br>
      *Memory size RAM: 8GB RAM<br>
      *Hard Drive Storage:512GB SSD<br>
      <br>
      Baliadanga Girl’s School<br>
      *Network: Wi-Fi and mobile hotspot connectivity<br>
      *Dell Laptops Older Models -3 Units<br>
      *Processor type and speed: Intel Core i3 Older generation<br>
      *Memory size RAM :4GB RAM<br>
      *Hard Drive (Storage) :12GB Storage<br>
      *Network: Wi-Fi and mobile hotspot connectivity<br>
      Topology Type : Ster topology (Wireless/Hotspot based)<br>
      *How it works:<br>
      *In our setup, a mobile phone acts as a mobile hotspot (or wireless access
      point )<br>
      which works like a central router.<br>
      *All 5 laptops (Hp and Dell )are wirelessly connected to this central
      mobile<br>
      hotspot to share the internet and access the network /server.</p>
    
  </body>
</html>
